Package: mosaicresid
Type: Package
Title: Residual-Shaded Mosaic Plots for 'ggplot2'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Sam", "Butler", email = "swmbutler@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A 'ggplot2'-native alternative to the shaded mosaic plots
    drawn by mosaicplot() in base 'R'. geom_mosaic_resid() maps two
    categorical variables with ordinary 'ggplot2' aesthetics, recursively
    partitions the unit square into tiles sized by their joint proportions,
    computes Pearson, deviance, or Freeman-Tukey residuals against a two-way
    independence model, and maps the residuals to fill color. It works on raw
    data, already aggregated counts, or contingency tables, and the tile
    geometry and residuals are also returned as a data frame by
    compute_mosaic_residuals().
